record lege-ecosystem.encode-quality.evidence.jp2lam-display-floor-corpus-2026-09-05/1 : evidence {
    title "Third Opus subagent. Low-target oracle re-sweep (7 x 0.8 MP, body fractions down to 0.05, targets 60-80, 245 new probes) closed the censored-crossing gap: prior_body_fraction refit with a quadratic ln(loss) term, per-target bias at 60/70 went from -16%/-9% to ~0, pooled sd ln 0.175 -> 0.165. Cheapest rung at 60/65/70 is within 1-5% across q50-q90 so outer_rungs_for_target unchanged. Probes on 7 photos x 70-90 x Fast/Balanced: 2.486 -> 2.386 (Fast 2.00, Balanced 2.77), zero misses. Display-floor corpus (11 photos x floors 60-80 x plain/eink400x300/eink600x450/tablet800x600, 220 cells): on 0.8 MP, floor 70 eink 600x450 costs 0.49x plain q75 Fast bytes and delivers 75.6 at display size (source-resolution score 51); eink 400x300 floor 70 = 0.33x (source-res 32); tablet 800x600 floor 70 = 0.64x (source-res 62). 4-6 MP sources into 400x300: 0.08-0.13x with source-resolution scores near or below zero. Display targets: 17.6% accept the first probe, rest 2 probes, 6/165 needed a rescue. Found and fixed 6 hard PerceptualTargetMissed failures: the display metric is non-monotone in body bytes at heavy downscale, so the single correction could land infeasible; backend now adds one rescue probe at the rung ceiling (honest SaturatedTop if it misses). Rescue streams are fat (1.2-4.4 MB) because display_prior_scale is fitted at 0.8 MP only; a 4-6 MP display-crossing sweep would supply the source-size term (ponytail comment). Recommendation recorded in for_quality/for_display docs: default e-ink floor 70 (byte cost per point turns over between 65 and 75), same floor for tablet since the larger panel is already stricter. New examples: perceptual_display.rs, perceptual_probes.rs; perceptual_oracle gained --fractions. Combined-tree gates: lib 381/381 serial, all integration targets, CLI 12/12, fmt clean."
    state verified
    result pass
    method command
    observed_at git:df6bb8cf45e9ee68a6544bbaf9e9136f6cd171d2
    command "cargo run --release --example perceptual_oracle -- test-set --qualities 50,60,70,75,80,85,90 --fractions 1.0,0.7,0.5,0.35,0.25,0.20,0.16,0.12,0.08,0.05 && cargo run --release --example perceptual_display && cargo run --release --example perceptual_probes && cargo test --lib -- --test-threads=1 && cargo test --no-fail-fast --test '*' && cargo test --features cli --bin jp2lam"
    artifact "lege-codecs/jp2lam/examples/perceptual_display.rs"
    summary """
        Third Opus subagent. Low-target oracle re-sweep (7 x 0.8 MP, body fractions down to 0.05, targets 60-80, 245 new probes) closed the censored-crossing gap: prior_body_fraction refit with a quadratic ln(loss) term, per-target bias at 60/70 went from -16%/-9% to ~0, pooled sd ln 0.175 -> 0.165. Cheapest rung at 60/65/70 is within 1-5% across q50-q90 so outer_rungs_for_target unchanged. Probes on 7 photos x 70-90 x Fast/Balanced: 2.486 -> 2.386 (Fast 2.00, Balanced 2.77), zero misses. Display-floor corpus (11 photos x floors 60-80 x plain/eink400x300/eink600x450/tablet800x600, 220 cells): on 0.8 MP, floor 70 eink 600x450 costs 0.49x plain q75 Fast bytes and delivers 75.6 at display size (source-resolution score 51); eink 400x300 floor 70 = 0.33x (source-res 32); tablet 800x600 floor 70 = 0.64x (source-res 62). 4-6 MP sources into 400x300: 0.08-0.13x with source-resolution scores near or below zero. Display targets: 17.6% accept the first probe, rest 2 probes, 6/165 needed a rescue. Found and fixed 6 hard PerceptualTargetMissed failures: the display metric is non-monotone in body bytes at heavy downscale, so the single correction could land infeasible; backend now adds one rescue probe at the rung ceiling (honest SaturatedTop if it misses). Rescue streams are fat (1.2-4.4 MB) because display_prior_scale is fitted at 0.8 MP only; a 4-6 MP display-crossing sweep would supply the source-size term (ponytail comment). Recommendation recorded in for_quality/for_display docs: default e-ink floor 70 (byte cost per point turns over between 65 and 75), same floor for tablet since the larger panel is already stricter. New examples: perceptual_display.rs, perceptual_probes.rs; perceptual_oracle gained --fractions. Combined-tree gates: lib 381/381 serial, all integration targets, CLI 12/12, fmt clean.
        """
}

record lege-ecosystem.encode-quality.evidence.jp2lam-large-source-and-display-term-2026-09-05/1 : evidence {
    title "Opus subagent, navigation. Large-source low-fraction re-sweep (4 x 4-6 MP + 12 MP, fractions to 0.05) -> 704 crossings / 12 sources. prior_body_fraction refit with a third per-source term ln(highpass energy per coefficient) from the same DWT-cache pass (source_band_stats): LOSO sd 0.212 (q+loss) -> 0.146; collinearity between near-zero and ln bytes resolved (stable fold ranges, no sign flips); large-source first-probe bias -0.138 -> -0.027. All features normalised per coefficient (gray sources have 1/3 the samples; per-pixel normalisation made the first probe ~2.5x too fat on gray). crossing_ratio() replaces the loss^(1/0.9) power law in aim/shrink (that law was biased -0.135..-0.415 in ln at high targets); EXPANSION_MARGIN 1.25 -> 1.00 wins on both corpora, constant deleted. display_prior_scale refit on band energies (LOSO 0.871 -> 0.247, under the 0.35 bar). Display budget 1 probe + 2 corrections. Box==source case root-caused (per-pixel normalisation + single correction stranded under floor): gray photo now byte-identical to plain Quality at the same floor; 11-source box==source 0.96x plain bytes; worst 1.33x is a text render (content absent from the oracle corpus). Results: 0.8 MP Fast 1.43 -> 1.29 probes, Balanced 1.89, all 1.59; 4-6 MP Fast 2.25, Balanced 3.17, all 2.92 -> 2.71; display 165 cells 1.65 -> 1.82 probes for -9.3% bytes and overshoot +6.4 -> +3.5; zero misses. Remaining 4-6 MP cost is accept-band bound (residual ~6 score points vs 2.7-point band). Combined-tree gates: jp2lam lib 381/381 serial, all integration targets, CLI 12/12, all targets build; lege check + test 339+19 pass."
    state verified
    result pass
    method command
    observed_at git:df6bb8cf45e9ee68a6544bbaf9e9136f6cd171d2
    command "cargo run --release --example perceptual_oracle -- test-set/test-set-4mp --fractions ..0.05 && cargo run --release --example perceptual_probes && cargo run --release --example perceptual_display && cargo test --lib -- --test-threads=1"
    artifact "lege-codecs/jp2lam/src/encode/ssim.rs"
    summary """
        Opus subagent, navigation. Large-source low-fraction re-sweep (4 x 4-6 MP + 12 MP, fractions to 0.05) -> 704 crossings / 12 sources. prior_body_fraction refit with a third per-source term ln(highpass energy per coefficient) from the same DWT-cache pass (source_band_stats): LOSO sd 0.212 (q+loss) -> 0.146; collinearity between near-zero and ln bytes resolved (stable fold ranges, no sign flips); large-source first-probe bias -0.138 -> -0.027. All features normalised per coefficient (gray sources have 1/3 the samples; per-pixel normalisation made the first probe ~2.5x too fat on gray). crossing_ratio() replaces the loss^(1/0.9) power law in aim/shrink (that law was biased -0.135..-0.415 in ln at high targets); EXPANSION_MARGIN 1.25 -> 1.00 wins on both corpora, constant deleted. display_prior_scale refit on band energies (LOSO 0.871 -> 0.247, under the 0.35 bar). Display budget 1 probe + 2 corrections. Box==source case root-caused (per-pixel normalisation + single correction stranded under floor): gray photo now byte-identical to plain Quality at the same floor; 11-source box==source 0.96x plain bytes; worst 1.33x is a text render (content absent from the oracle corpus). Results: 0.8 MP Fast 1.43 -> 1.29 probes, Balanced 1.89, all 1.59; 4-6 MP Fast 2.25, Balanced 3.17, all 2.92 -> 2.71; display 165 cells 1.65 -> 1.82 probes for -9.3% bytes and overshoot +6.4 -> +3.5; zero misses. Remaining 4-6 MP cost is accept-band bound (residual ~6 score points vs 2.7-point band). Combined-tree gates: jp2lam lib 381/381 serial, all integration targets, CLI 12/12, all targets build; lege check + test 339+19 pass.
        """
}

