record lege-ecosystem.encode-quality.evidence.jp2lam-probe-reduction-and-display-preset-2026-09-05/1 : evidence {
    title "Two Opus subagents. (A) JPXL probe history reviewed (jpxl-encode-policy quality.rs / quality_prediction.rs: crossing predictor b57c9d4..0885915, trusted first probe ea65364/488770b, gated direct correction, reserve-coupled accept band a2b7071; JPXL's own record 22be3b9 calls the last stretch predictor-bound). Ported to jp2lam: first-probe predictor as a fraction of the rung's total Tier-1 body bytes (prior_body_fraction; sd ln 0.06-0.11 vs 0.33-0.40 for the bpp prior), reserve-coupled aim/accept band replacing ACCEPT_OVERSHOOT, trusted outer-rung stop, display-aware prior scale sqrt(display px/source px), PERCEPTUAL_PROBES counter + examples/perceptual_probes.rs. 7 photos x {70,75,80,85,90} x {Fast,Balanced}: probes 4.386 -> 2.486 (Fast 3.457 -> 2.086, Balanced 5.314 -> 2.886), bytes geomean x0.977, zero floor misses; Fast 11/35 cells in one probe. 4-6 MP after-only 3.04 probes. (B) DisplayProfile{max_width,max_height,color: Eink|Tablet}, PerceptualTarget::for_display(score, display, effort) with display: Option<DisplayProfile>, StreamEvaluator::for_display/for_target (box downscale in linear light + luminance fold, identity when the image fits a colour box), QualityBudget::for_target = 2 evaluations for display targets, EncodeOptions::display_photo, CLI --display eink:WxH|tablet:WxH (Fast default). q75 --display eink:400x300 on 1024x768 photos: 28,004 B / 59,516 B (display score 78.8 / 78.3, 2 probes) vs plain q75 88,644 / 176,408 B. Gates: lib 381/381 serial, perceptual_api 9/9, CLI 12/12, all targets build. Known gap: oracle sweep floor body fraction 0.25 censors crossings below target ~75, so prior is extrapolated there; third agent re-sweeping."
    state verified
    result pass
    method command
    observed_at git:df6bb8cf45e9ee68a6544bbaf9e9136f6cd171d2
    command "cargo test --lib -- --test-threads=1 && cargo test --test perceptual_api && cargo test --features cli --bin jp2lam && cargo run --release --example perceptual_probes"
    artifact "lege-codecs/jp2lam/src/encode/ssim.rs"
    summary """
        Two Opus subagents. (A) JPXL probe history reviewed (jpxl-encode-policy quality.rs / quality_prediction.rs: crossing predictor b57c9d4..0885915, trusted first probe ea65364/488770b, gated direct correction, reserve-coupled accept band a2b7071; JPXL's own record 22be3b9 calls the last stretch predictor-bound). Ported to jp2lam: first-probe predictor as a fraction of the rung's total Tier-1 body bytes (prior_body_fraction; sd ln 0.06-0.11 vs 0.33-0.40 for the bpp prior), reserve-coupled aim/accept band replacing ACCEPT_OVERSHOOT, trusted outer-rung stop, display-aware prior scale sqrt(display px/source px), PERCEPTUAL_PROBES counter + examples/perceptual_probes.rs. 7 photos x {70,75,80,85,90} x {Fast,Balanced}: probes 4.386 -> 2.486 (Fast 3.457 -> 2.086, Balanced 5.314 -> 2.886), bytes geomean x0.977, zero floor misses; Fast 11/35 cells in one probe. 4-6 MP after-only 3.04 probes. (B) DisplayProfile{max_width,max_height,color: Eink|Tablet}, PerceptualTarget::for_display(score, display, effort) with display: Option<DisplayProfile>, StreamEvaluator::for_display/for_target (box downscale in linear light + luminance fold, identity when the image fits a colour box), QualityBudget::for_target = 2 evaluations for display targets, EncodeOptions::display_photo, CLI --display eink:WxH|tablet:WxH (Fast default). q75 --display eink:400x300 on 1024x768 photos: 28,004 B / 59,516 B (display score 78.8 / 78.3, 2 probes) vs plain q75 88,644 / 176,408 B. Gates: lib 381/381 serial, perceptual_api 9/9, CLI 12/12, all targets build. Known gap: oracle sweep floor body fraction 0.25 censors crossings below target ~75, so prior is extrapolated there; third agent re-sweeping.
        """
}

record lege-ecosystem.encode-quality.evidence.jp2lam-probe-usage-1-5-2026-09-05/1 : evidence {
    title "Opus subagent, probe usage. First-probe predictor prior_body_fraction gained per-source terms available for free in the search: near-zero coefficient fraction of the unquantized DWT (computed from the cache, or per-tile recompute on the memory-capped path so the cache stays winner-invariant) and ln(body bytes/pixel); leave-one-source-out sd ln 0.186 -> 0.115 over 12 sources. First probe now aims at floor+reserve. display_prior_scale refit on 112 converged display crossings: ln scale = -4.4888 + 0.5234 ln(display px) - 0.2009 ln(source px) + 0.15, clamped [ratio,1] (fitted on 9 groups sd 0.19; two soft large sources sit ~10x lower, residual sd 0.75 over all 11, documented). Balanced reserve 0.03 -> 0.045 (-0.63 probes for +0.5% bytes); Fast keeps reserve 0.06 with a 3x accept band (JPXL good-enough band). Results 7 x 0.8 MP x floors 70-90: Fast 2.00 -> 1.43 probes (+1.5% bytes, 77% one-probe), Balanced 2.77 -> 1.91 (+0.5%, 49% one-probe), all 2.39 -> 1.67, zero misses. 4-6 MP source-resolution: Fast 2.42 / Balanced 3.42 (weak spot: oracle never bracketed below body fraction 0.25 there). Display corpus 165 cells: 1.86 -> 1.65 probes, mean bytes 262.5 -> 135.2 KB (-48%), 4-6 MP 520 -> 202 KB, rescues 5 -> 0, misses 0, one-probe 17.8% -> 35.4%. Gates: lib 381/381 serial, perceptual_api 11/11, metric_identity 3/3, CLI 12/12, all targets build."
    state verified
    result pass
    method command
    observed_at git:df6bb8cf45e9ee68a6544bbaf9e9136f6cd171d2
    command "cargo run --release --example perceptual_probes && cargo run --release --example perceptual_display && cargo test --lib -- --test-threads=1 && cargo test --test perceptual_api --test metric_identity"
    artifact "lege-codecs/jp2lam/src/encode/ssim.rs"
    summary """
        Opus subagent, probe usage. First-probe predictor prior_body_fraction gained per-source terms available for free in the search: near-zero coefficient fraction of the unquantized DWT (computed from the cache, or per-tile recompute on the memory-capped path so the cache stays winner-invariant) and ln(body bytes/pixel); leave-one-source-out sd ln 0.186 -> 0.115 over 12 sources. First probe now aims at floor+reserve. display_prior_scale refit on 112 converged display crossings: ln scale = -4.4888 + 0.5234 ln(display px) - 0.2009 ln(source px) + 0.15, clamped [ratio,1] (fitted on 9 groups sd 0.19; two soft large sources sit ~10x lower, residual sd 0.75 over all 11, documented). Balanced reserve 0.03 -> 0.045 (-0.63 probes for +0.5% bytes); Fast keeps reserve 0.06 with a 3x accept band (JPXL good-enough band). Results 7 x 0.8 MP x floors 70-90: Fast 2.00 -> 1.43 probes (+1.5% bytes, 77% one-probe), Balanced 2.77 -> 1.91 (+0.5%, 49% one-probe), all 2.39 -> 1.67, zero misses. 4-6 MP source-resolution: Fast 2.42 / Balanced 3.42 (weak spot: oracle never bracketed below body fraction 0.25 there). Display corpus 165 cells: 1.86 -> 1.65 probes, mean bytes 262.5 -> 135.2 KB (-48%), 4-6 MP 520 -> 202 KB, rescues 5 -> 0, misses 0, one-probe 17.8% -> 35.4%. Gates: lib 381/381 serial, perceptual_api 11/11, metric_identity 3/3, CLI 12/12, all targets build.
        """
}

record lege-ecosystem.encode-quality.evidence.jp2lam-resampled-floor-exact-2026-09-05/1 : evidence {
    title "Opus subagent. Resampled display encodes now verify the floor against the ORIGINAL source: EncodeContext carries metric_reference (the un-resampled view) set by prepared_context() in encode/mod.rs; the search builds StreamEvaluator::for_target(context.metric_source(), ..) so the original is conditioned into the display box and candidates (decoded at the resampled/metric size) are scored through score_display_sized_candidate. last_achieved_score() (thread-local) exposes the encoder's winning score; display_resample_bench asserts encoder == reader-visible score within 1e-6 on all 22 rows (max gap before 0.05, now 0.00). New test resampled_display_encode_scores_the_original_exactly. linear_row fast path shared by fill_linear_from_view and box_downscale_view cut both full-source passes ~35% (box downscale 63 -> 41 ms on 6 MP). Net cost of the exact floor ~+3% encode time; bytes +0.015%; decode unchanged. resampled/source-res: bytes 0.458x, encode 0.276x, decode 0.328x. Gates: lib 381/381 serial, all integration targets (perceptual_api 12), CLI 12/12, all targets build. Left: evaluator rebuilds the conditioned reference (45 ms) although box_downscale_view computed the same planes; sharing them would cost the bit-exact identity."
    state verified
    result pass
    method command
    observed_at git:df6bb8cf45e9ee68a6544bbaf9e9136f6cd171d2
    command "cargo test --lib -- --test-threads=1 && cargo test --no-fail-fast --test '*' && cargo run --release --example display_resample_bench"
    artifact "lege-codecs/jp2lam/src/encode/context.rs"
    summary """
        Opus subagent. Resampled display encodes now verify the floor against the ORIGINAL source: EncodeContext carries metric_reference (the un-resampled view) set by prepared_context() in encode/mod.rs; the search builds StreamEvaluator::for_target(context.metric_source(), ..) so the original is conditioned into the display box and candidates (decoded at the resampled/metric size) are scored through score_display_sized_candidate. last_achieved_score() (thread-local) exposes the encoder's winning score; display_resample_bench asserts encoder == reader-visible score within 1e-6 on all 22 rows (max gap before 0.05, now 0.00). New test resampled_display_encode_scores_the_original_exactly. linear_row fast path shared by fill_linear_from_view and box_downscale_view cut both full-source passes ~35% (box downscale 63 -> 41 ms on 6 MP). Net cost of the exact floor ~+3% encode time; bytes +0.015%; decode unchanged. resampled/source-res: bytes 0.458x, encode 0.276x, decode 0.328x. Gates: lib 381/381 serial, all integration targets (perceptual_api 12), CLI 12/12, all targets build. Left: evaluator rebuilds the conditioned reference (45 ms) although box_downscale_view computed the same planes; sharing them would cost the bit-exact identity.
        """
}

record lege-ecosystem.encode-quality.evidence.jp2lam-small-image-and-resample-2026-09-05/1 : evidence {
    title "Opus subagent, small-image encoding. Profile (release, 7 photos box-downscaled to 64x48..640x480): JP2 boxes 85 B + main header 78-96 B are already minimal; decomposition levels already shrink (loosening the LL>=16 rule was worse, reverted); rayon spin-up and tile policy are not costs; perceptual time is T1 + reconstruct + ssimulacra2 + evaluator construction. Fixes: 256-entry sRGB->linear LUT replacing powf per sample (bit-exact; evaluator_new -32%, score_decoded -27%, 640x480 display encode -16%; perceptual encodes 5-15% faster with identical bytes), e-ink luma fold before resampling, sources below the metric's 8x8 floor resolve to Lossless instead of failing, aggregated profile scopes. Opt-in resample-to-display source path: DisplayProfile.resample_source / resampling_source(), encoded_size(), RESAMPLE_MIN_FACTOR 1.25, downscale in linear light (sRGB-space averaging failed the reader-visible floor by 0.25), CLI --resample, StreamEvaluator::score_display_sized_candidate for reader-view verification. Floor 70 into e-ink 600x450, 11 photos: resampled/source-res bytes 0.46x, encode 0.25x, decode 0.31x, probes unchanged, minimum reader-visible score 71.2 (4-6 MP: 285 KB/1.5 s -> 74 KB/0.16 s). Caveat: in the resampled path the encoder's own floor is verified against the resampled source; reader-visible floor holds empirically (min margin 1.2). Combined-tree gates: lib 381/381 serial, all integration targets, CLI 12/12, all targets build warning-free, fmt clean, cargo check -p lege ok."
    state verified
    result pass
    method command
    observed_at git:df6bb8cf45e9ee68a6544bbaf9e9136f6cd171d2
    command "cargo run --release --features profile --example small_image_bench && cargo run --release --example display_resample_bench && cargo test --lib -- --test-threads=1 && cargo test --no-fail-fast --test '*' && cargo check -p lege"
    artifact "lege-codecs/jp2lam/src/encode/mod.rs"
    summary """
        Opus subagent, small-image encoding. Profile (release, 7 photos box-downscaled to 64x48..640x480): JP2 boxes 85 B + main header 78-96 B are already minimal; decomposition levels already shrink (loosening the LL>=16 rule was worse, reverted); rayon spin-up and tile policy are not costs; perceptual time is T1 + reconstruct + ssimulacra2 + evaluator construction. Fixes: 256-entry sRGB->linear LUT replacing powf per sample (bit-exact; evaluator_new -32%, score_decoded -27%, 640x480 display encode -16%; perceptual encodes 5-15% faster with identical bytes), e-ink luma fold before resampling, sources below the metric's 8x8 floor resolve to Lossless instead of failing, aggregated profile scopes. Opt-in resample-to-display source path: DisplayProfile.resample_source / resampling_source(), encoded_size(), RESAMPLE_MIN_FACTOR 1.25, downscale in linear light (sRGB-space averaging failed the reader-visible floor by 0.25), CLI --resample, StreamEvaluator::score_display_sized_candidate for reader-view verification. Floor 70 into e-ink 600x450, 11 photos: resampled/source-res bytes 0.46x, encode 0.25x, decode 0.31x, probes unchanged, minimum reader-visible score 71.2 (4-6 MP: 285 KB/1.5 s -> 74 KB/0.16 s). Caveat: in the resampled path the encoder's own floor is verified against the resampled source; reader-visible floor holds empirically (min margin 1.2). Combined-tree gates: lib 381/381 serial, all integration targets, CLI 12/12, all targets build warning-free, fmt clean, cargo check -p lege ok.
        """
}

record lege-ecosystem.encode-quality.evidence.jp2lam-ssim-ladder-tuning-2026-09-05/1 : evidence {
    title "Session 8c tuning from the oracle sweep (12 full-grid + 7 Q50-screen sources, ssimulacra2-jpxl-1). Byte-cheapest outer quantizer depends on target, not source: q60 at 80, q60-75 at 85-90, q50 at 95 (all-pass ceiling 95.3-96.5), q70-75 at 97.5, q85+ at 98+; q99 never cheapest (q95 already scores 100 all-pass). Fixed [75,90,99] cost +24% bytes at 80, +6% at 95. Production now uses outer_rungs_for_target (5 target bands). Also fixed a pre-existing inner PCRD navigation failure: the loss-domain crossing fit crept <1%/probe from just under target when the feasible side was the far ceiling, exhausting Fast/Balanced budgets and shipping the ceiling stream (20240501_110934 at 80 emitted 1,012,985 bytes on the old ladder); MIN_BRACKET_STEP=1.05 forces a minimum relative climb. After: 192515 t80 107,222 B (was 452,663 new ladder / lucky 104,607 old), 110934 t80 211,876 B (was 1,012,985), t90 219,530 / 341,200 B. Lib 375/375 serial; all integration targets green; encode::ssim_dwt counter test races under parallel runner (pre-existing, papercut logged)."
    state verified
    result pass
    method command
    observed_at git:df6bb8cf45e9ee68a6544bbaf9e9136f6cd171d2
    command "cargo test --lib -- --test-threads=1 && cargo test --no-fail-fast --test '*' && target/release/jp2lam encode test-set/{20240502_192515,20240501_110934}.png --ssimulacra2 {80,90}"
    artifact "lege-codecs/jp2lam/src/encode/ssim.rs"
    summary """
        Session 8c tuning from the oracle sweep (12 full-grid + 7 Q50-screen sources, ssimulacra2-jpxl-1). Byte-cheapest outer quantizer depends on target, not source: q60 at 80, q60-75 at 85-90, q50 at 95 (all-pass ceiling 95.3-96.5), q70-75 at 97.5, q85+ at 98+; q99 never cheapest (q95 already scores 100 all-pass). Fixed [75,90,99] cost +24% bytes at 80, +6% at 95. Production now uses outer_rungs_for_target (5 target bands). Also fixed a pre-existing inner PCRD navigation failure: the loss-domain crossing fit crept <1%/probe from just under target when the feasible side was the far ceiling, exhausting Fast/Balanced budgets and shipping the ceiling stream (20240501_110934 at 80 emitted 1,012,985 bytes on the old ladder); MIN_BRACKET_STEP=1.05 forces a minimum relative climb. After: 192515 t80 107,222 B (was 452,663 new ladder / lucky 104,607 old), 110934 t80 211,876 B (was 1,012,985), t90 219,530 / 341,200 B. Lib 375/375 serial; all integration targets green; encode::ssim_dwt counter test races under parallel runner (pre-existing, papercut logged).
        """
}

