record lege-ecosystem.evidence.lege-pdf-agent-text-layout-fixes-tests/1 : evidence {
    title "lege-pdf text fixes: word gaps between show operators, row clustering, paragraph blocks; 199 tests pass"
    state verified
    result pass
    method command
    observed_at git:35ab93d1ce539610b43d0062a6fb27b7fb89256a
    command "cargo test -p lege-pdf-agent -p pdf-text -p pdf-read -p lege-pdf-read -p pdf-chaos-tests"
    summary """
        25 test binaries, 199 passed, 0 failed on the working tree over HEAD (2026-11-05). Changes verified: pdf-text now puts a space between two show operators whose advance boxes stand a quarter of the wider advance apart (was a full glyph width between ink boxes, which dropped the space at a font switch: '(orembedded)' on taubman2000.pdf p.2); the agent clusters words into rows by band overlap, so superscripts and stray punctuation stay on their line; blocks break at line-step changes, short last lines, first-line indents and list markers; a loosely justified line is one run of words in the physical layout. Words differing from Poppler 26.10 pdftotext, before -> after (only-ours / only-Poppler): 13-page paper 124/183 -> 64/69; 164-page spec 970/1220 -> 812/1133; 650-page book 4885/4450 -> 4382/3114; 782-page scan unchanged. Whole-document text timings unchanged (book 334/343 ms, scan 385/397 ms min/median). Build check: 'cargo install --path lege-pdf/agent --locked' (release, 4m24s) and the same with --profile debug-fast both yield a binary that answers initialize, tools/list (10 tools) and tools/call; 'claude mcp list' reports it Connected.
        Capture "C:\\Users\\dkoep\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\631b5a07a712c8b2\\d04edd3f-2065-4f1b-8237-c01ac029729d\\scratchpad\\final_tests2.txt": 18031 bytes; sha256:6b2cb99e36e81188278de62f5bf2487d6a5dea9c73f6c45f53cc3cd98161568c (identity only; raw capture is not a retained artifact).
        """
    author "dk"
}

