record lege-ecosystem.evidence.stale-observation-requeue-20260908/1 : evidence {
    title "2026-09-08 re-verification of the stale observation queue"
    state verified
    result pass
    method manual
    observed_at git:823d46ddc946bb5d6ac8fc360a9d9ba6506d7a7d
    summary """
        The ledger-cleanup pass of 2026-09-08 re-read every observation the review queue had
        marked stale against the source at HEAD 823d46dd, and re-observed the ones that still
        hold. Confirmed still true: symbol mode is still the Jbig2Config default with a bit-exact
        generic opt-out (lege-codecs/jbig2enc-rust/src/encode/structs.rs:178,243); the three inert
        jbig2enc config fields still have no reader outside structs.rs and match_tolerance is
        still gated behind text_refine (encode/document.rs:451); the ten TrueTyping/halftone review
        fixes landed in 32abd79d and 12e08f7a and are present (color_processing.rs:14,24,
        glyphfont.rs:118,194, pdf_artifact.rs:388, truetype_writer.rs:222); all four PP-OCRv6 WGPU
        blockers remain fixed (lege-gpu/src/vision/onnx/load.rs:65,255, lower.rs:93,126); the
        jbig2enc-py round-trip tests still exist (tests/test_jbig2enc.py:320,330,352) though the
        wheel moved 0.5.4 -> 0.6.0 in 1f0b36f9; the Windows OCR benchmark's measured code path
        still exists; DocLayout is still bypassed by perform_page_rgb_ocr (lege-process/ocr/fast.rs:52);
        clean_page_for_mrc is unchanged (lege-process/core/clean_gray.rs:364,412); the parallel
        glyph-dictionary probe is intact (glyphfont.rs:387,1295,2372); and per-occurrence baseline
        handling with its regression test is in place (glyphfont.rs:3007,1618,4087). The absolute
        benchmark numbers inside those statements were not re-measured, only the mechanisms they
        describe. Three observations did not survive and were superseded rather than re-observed:
        truetyping-letters-ride-off-their-baseline (the RISE_SNAP_PX/VARIANT_JOIN_PX snap window it
        describes no longer exists; glyphfont.rs:1390 is now an exact descent comparison),
        truetyping-halftone-review-20260905 (its closing "no application fixes made" is no longer
        true) and ocr-v5-v6-recipe-20260820 (its "not a viable v6 replacement yet" verdict was
        already contradicted by the resolved-blockers observation that cites it).
        """
}

